    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15518" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-lŏco</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to let</i> or <i>hire
				out</i>, <i>to let out to farm</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Verr. 2, 3, 22</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bovem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					1, 7, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">funus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 3, 7, § 10</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sese curandum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 26,
					1, 3, § 4</span></i>
			.—<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gentem Judaeorum, i. q. ejus vectigalia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 28 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
